From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Seedance: generate from ModelArk Asset Library ids, not
 inline sheets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Seedance 2.x screens every inline reference image for real people, and a
photorealistic character sheet is rejected as a possible real person even
when it is entirely AI-generated:

  InputImageSensitiveContentDetected.PrivacyInformation
  The input image content[1] may contain a real person.

No prompt wording avoids it — the check runs on the picture. The sanctioned
fix is ByteDance's private virtual portrait library: the image is reviewed
once at upload, and generations then carry asset://<id>, which the model
already trusts.

  - lib/ark/signer.ts   Volcengine V4 request signing for the Assets API,
                        which is a signed top-level OpenAPI service (AK/SK),
                        not the bearer token the models use.
  - lib/ark/assets.ts   CreateAssetGroup / CreateAsset / GetAsset /
                        DeleteAsset, activation polling, credential storage.
  - videoGen/providers/ark.ts
                        Direct ModelArk Seedance provider. Asset ids go out
                        as asset://<id> and are named positionally in the
                        prompt (@Image1...); inline images are the fallback,
                        never the default.
  - characterAssets.ts  Registration orchestration: one asset group per
                        character, one asset per costume, status recorded on
                        the row. Best-effort and off the request path — a
                        character stays creatable and usable via the keyframe
                        route when ModelArk is unconfigured or rejects a sheet.

Character clips take the asset route when the provider can use it, which also
drops the per-scene keyframe generation. Identity-locked jobs deliberately do
not fail over to providers that ignore asset ids: a substitute would return a
well-formed clip of the wrong person, which is worse than a retryable failure.

Also: admin card for credentials and per-character status with a retry, and a
backfill script for characters created before this.

