++# Seedance Asset Library — integration guide
++
++Fixes `InputImageSensitiveContentDetected.PrivacyInformation` ("the input image `content[1]` may contain a real person") by registering character sheets with ByteDance once, and generating from the returned asset id instead of the image.
++
++## The problem this solves
++
++Seedance 2.x screens every reference image in a generation request for real people. A photorealistic character sheet trips that filter **even when it is entirely AI-generated** — which is why Replicate and OpenRouter also reject them. There is no prompt wording that gets around it, because the check runs on the picture, not the prompt.
++
++The sanctioned fix is ByteDance's **private virtual portrait library**: the image is reviewed once at upload, and from then on the request carries `asset://<id>`, which the model already trusts. One review per character instead of a moderation gamble per scene.
++
++Asset ids are scoped to the ModelArk account that minted them. An asset created under a reseller's account (Atlas Cloud, Higgsfield) is unusable with your key, and vice versa — this only works with a direct BytePlus/ModelArk account.
++
++## Apply it
++
++From the repo root:
++
++```bash
++git apply --check seedance-asset-library.patch   # dry run — should print nothing
++git am seedance-asset-library.patch              # applies as one commit
++```
++
++Then:
++
++```bash
++pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push   # 5 new nullable columns, additive, no data loss
++pnpm run build
++```
++
++No new npm dependencies. Generated API clients are included in the patch.
++
++## Configuration
++
++Two different credentials, and mixing them up is the most likely first failure:
++
++| What | Used for | Where |
++|---|---|---|
++| `ARK_API_KEY` (bearer token) | Generating video | Admin → video gen settings, or the env secret |
++| `ARK_ACCESS_KEY_ID` + `ARK_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` (AK/SK pair) | The Asset Library API | Admin → ModelArk Asset Library card, or the env secrets |
++
++The Assets API is a signed top-level OpenAPI service, so it needs the key pair — a bearer token will not authenticate it.
++
++Optional overrides: `ARK_BASE_URL` (default `https://ark.ap-southeast.bytepluses.com/api/v3`), `ARK_ASSETS_HOST` (default `open.byteplusapi.com`), `ARK_ASSETS_REGION` (default `ap-southeast-1`).
++
++### Prerequisites on the ModelArk account
++
++Neither can be done from code, and both surface as a readable error on the admin card:
++
++1. **Advanced Creation Rights** must be activated. The capacity quota is shared between the virtual portrait and real-human libraries.
++2. **The first asset group requires an authorization letter** signed in the ModelArk console.
++
++### Selecting the provider
++
++Admin → video gen settings → provider `ByteDance ModelArk`. Defaults to Seedance 2.5 (`dreamina-seedance-2-5-260628`) for both engines; Seedance 2.0 and 2.0 Fast are in the dropdown. Asset ids are only used on this provider — every other provider ignores them and falls back to the existing keyframe path, so switching back changes nothing.
++
++## How it behaves
++
++**Registration** runs automatically and in the background when a character or a costume is created. The response returns immediately; the asset lands about a minute later. Every outcome is written to the outfit row, so a failure is visible rather than silent.
++
++**Generation** takes one of two routes, decided per clip:
++
++- *Asset route* — ModelArk selected and the outfit's asset is `Active`: the ids go straight into the request and **no per-scene keyframe is generated**. One fewer image call per scene, and no generation-to-generation face drift.
++- *Keyframe route* — everything else: unchanged from today.
++
++**Failover is deliberately blocked for identity-locked jobs.** If ModelArk is down, a substitute provider would happily return a well-formed clip of the wrong person. A failed job the tenant can retry is the better outcome, so substitutes that cannot honour the lock are filtered out.
++
++**Deletes release the asset upstream** — capacity is a purchased, shared quota, so a character deleted in the app must not keep occupying a slot.
++
++## Backfill
++
++Characters created before this patch have no asset id. After building:
++
++```bash
++pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run backfill:ark-assets -- --dry-run
++pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run backfill:ark-assets
++pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run backfill:ark-assets -- --tenant 42   # one workspace
++pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run backfill:ark-assets -- --skip-failed # don't retry rejects
++```
++
++Safe to re-run: outfits already holding an `Active` asset are skipped, so a second pass only picks up what the first one missed. Sequential by design — `CreateAsset` is rate-limited per account.
++
++## Admin surface
++
++Admin → AI → **ModelArk Asset Library**: the AK/SK pair, and every character with its group id and per-outfit status (`Active` / `Processing` / `Failed` / not registered) plus the verbatim upstream error. **Register** re-runs registration for one character — the fix after you have activated rights, freed quota, or regenerated a sheet.
++
++## Image guidance
++
++ModelArk's own best practice, worth following since it also fixes face/costume consistency: 2+ stills per character in one group, vertical, one full-body frontal and one face close-up above the shoulders with a neutral expression and the face at roughly two-thirds of the frame. Limits: jpeg/png/webp/bmp/tiff/gif/heic, aspect ratio 0.4–2.5, 300–6000 px, under 30 MB.
++
++Assets must not resemble a real person. AI-generated originals qualify. A sheet that reads as an identifiable real human belongs in the real-human library instead — invite-only, and it requires that person to complete liveness verification on their own Volcengine account. This patch deliberately does not implement that path: it cannot be driven from a server.
++
++## New API surface
++
++`GET /admin/ark-assets`, `PUT|DELETE /admin/ark-assets/key`, `POST /admin/ark-assets/characters/{id}/register`. All superadmin-only. No tenant-facing contract changed.
++
++## Verified
++
++- `pnpm run typecheck:libs`, api-server and socialforge typechecks — clean
++- Spec lint clean; orval codegen additive only (no drift in existing operations)
++- `db push` applied cleanly against a fresh Postgres 16
++- 30 new tests (signer, provider, registration orchestration, admin card), existing character/video/admin suites green
++
++## Known limits
++
++- The real-human library is not implemented (see above).
++- Registration status is only visible in the admin surface, not the tenant-facing characters API — the tenant-facing contract was left untouched on purpose.
++- `waitForAssetActive` gives up after 5 minutes and records `Processing`; the admin Register button re-checks. There is no automatic re-poll sweep yet.
