++/**
++ * Registering characters in the ModelArk Asset Library.
++ *
++ * A character sheet sent inline is screened for real people on every
++ * generation; a photorealistic one is rejected as a possible real person even
++ * when it is entirely AI-generated. Registering the image once turns it into
++ * an asset id the model already trusts, and every later scene references the
++ * id instead of the picture.
++ *
++ * Registration is deliberately best-effort and off the critical path: it is
++ * an optimisation for one provider, so a character must still be creatable
++ * (and usable, via the keyframe path) when ModelArk is unconfigured, slow, or
++ * rejects the image. Every failure is recorded on the outfit row so the admin
